  "learn": {
    "title": "Range Sentry",
    "body": "Power HC-SR04 from VIN (5 V) and GND. TRIG goes to GPIO18. ECHO goes through 1 kΩ to a junction shared by GPIO19 and a 2.2 kΩ resistor to GND; never connect 5 V ECHO directly to GPIO19. Wire GPIO23 → 220 Ω → LED → GND.\n\nEvery 60 ms, send a 10 µs trigger pulse, use pulseIn(19, HIGH, 25000), and convert duration / 58.3 to centimeters. Keep the last five samples in a circular array. Copy and sort them, then use the middle value once five valid readings exist. A zero-duration timeout must clear the history and turn the LED off. Turn on when the median is below 50 cm; print MEDIAN=30;NEAR or MEDIAN=120;CLEAR using a whole number.\n\nSet distance to 120 cm before Run; wait one second, set 30 cm, wait one second, then set 200 cm. Expect clear, near, clear. One brief outlier among four far samples must not trigger. Also toggle the built-in GPIO2 LED every 100 ms (200 ms period) to show the loop still runs. pulseIn waits briefly for echo; use millis() for the other tasks.",
    "links": []
  },
